==English==

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|task|master}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-us-taskmaster.oga|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Someone who [[supervise]]s [[worker]]s, especially one who [[impose]]s [[hard]] or [[burdensome]] [[work]].
#* {{RQ:KJV|Exodus|3|7|text=And the Lord said, I have surely seen the affliction of my people which are in Egypt, and have heard their cry by reason of their '''taskmasters'''; for I know their sorrows}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} A [[source]] of [[hard]] [[work]] or [[responsibility]].
#* {{quote-web|1=en|date=June 4, 2023|author=Charles Hugh Smith|work=What Happens When the Competent Opt Out?|url=https://charleshughsmith.blogspot.com/2023/06/what-happens-when-competent-opt-out.html|text=It all looked so easy when the competent were at the helm, but reality is a cruel '''taskmaster''', and all the excuses that worked as an underling wear thin once the incompetent are in leadership roles.}}

